assistant: Subject: Follow next_cursor to fetch all search result pages

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 splits search results into pages. It returns the first 5 items along with `total: 7` and `next_cursor: "5"`, but `search_products` only made one request and ignored the cursor, so it returned 5 of 7 matches. The handler now keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` (the `cursor` parameter is already in the vendor's spec) and adds each page's items until there is no next cursor. Older v1 responses have no `next_cursor`, so they make the same single request and give the same output as before. Typecheck, lint and the other 13 tests pass. The repro test still fails, but not on the contract: it reports `UNMATCHED_REQUEST` because the recording never captured the second page (`GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5`). It will pass only after someone runs `fiks rerecord` to create `tr_d02358451e.rerecorded.json`. I couldn't run that here because only `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` are allowed. Separately, prices in this version look like cents (6900 instead of 69) and break `items.price.range`. That was outside this fix's target, so I left it alone.

